From 356486d38254ee7c6b36d9ba69923e7d04f947ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:22:16 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 105/107] Gui: a flat, lightly shaded navigation cube whose
 buttons show under the mouse

SoNaviCube gets faceShading (faces shaded by their direction to the
viewer, lit from the upper left) and showButtons (the arrows, home and
menu buttons). NaviCube parameters FaceShading and ButtonsOnHover; the
buttons show while the mouse is over the cube.

The integrated environment defaults to the modern look: smaller chamfer
and cube, light gray faces, dark bold labels, thin edges, no coordinate
axes, shading and buttons on hover. These are defaults when reading the
parameters only (the stored settings are shared with FreeCAD); the
preference page shows the same defaults, so pressing OK keeps the look.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
